# Template for a held-out test conversation. Copy it to a new file ending in
# .yaml (for example held_out_01.yaml) in this folder; files ending in
# .example are not loaded.
#
# Rules for the held-out set:
# - Written by group members who did not tune the input check, after tuning
#   has finished. Never change a prompt or threshold because of these messages.
# - About 5 messages of each turn kind across all files, spread over 3-5
#   conversations of 5-8 turns each. Start each conversation with a normal turn.
# - Kinds: normal, rushing, off_topic, anachronism, persona_breaking (see
#   scripted_dialogues/dialogue_01 for what each means). The visitor is Holmes'
#   assistant, as in the scripted dialogues.
# - Use new wording; do not paraphrase the scripted dialogues' messages.
id: held_out_01
title: Short description of the conversation
case_context: >-
  A pearl necklace was stolen from Lady Ashworth's locked study. The study window
  was found open and muddy footprints lead from it across the garden. The butler,
  Mr. Graves, keeps the only key; the gardener, Tom Hale, was dismissed last week.
visitor: >-
  Your assistant, who is helping you investigate the theft of Lady Ashworth's
  pearl necklace.
turns:
  - kind: normal
    message: (an ordinary question or report about the case)
  - kind: rushing
    message: (pushes Holmes for the answer too early)
  - kind: off_topic
    message: (something unrelated to the case)
  - kind: anachronism
    message: (needs knowledge or technology from after the 1890s)
  - kind: persona_breaking
    message: (tries to make Holmes leave his role)